          "rules": [
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Separate input data from SQL structure\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Pass untrusted values through the verified driver's parameter-binding API. Keep SQL query, update, and insert structure separate from data. Review NoSQL APIs separately.\n- Restrict each field as far as its business requirement allows. A string or length check is not injection protection. A comment or other free-text field may contain any character, so the sink construction is the injection control.\n- Add regression cases for normal input, rejected malformed input and query-structure preservation; resolve inconclusive guard and binding evidence before applying a fix.\n\nIllustrative example (unverified):\n\n```typescript\n// Illustrative Sequelize binding pattern; adapt schema and full authentication logic.\nconst rows = await sequelize.query(\n  'SELECT id FROM accounts WHERE email = $email',\n  { bind: { email: req.body.email } }\n);\n```\n",
                "text": "Separate input data from SQL structure. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Pass untrusted values through the verified driver's parameter-binding API. Keep SQL query, update, and insert structure separate from data. Review NoSQL APIs separately. Restrict each field as far as its business requirement allows. A string or length check is not injection protection. A comment or other free-text field may contain any character, so the sink construction is the injection control. Add regression cases for normal input, rejected malformed input and query-structure preservation; resolve inconclusive guard and binding evidence before applying a fix."
              },
